92186045585 true] [17592186152155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256764 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152156 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256785 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152158 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256779 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152158 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256780 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152158 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256781 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152158 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256782 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256742 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256743 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256744 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256745 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256748 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186148907 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186152401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256249 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152401 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152401 1071 "![](images/c2/c28d3a6098da6c8be022974e96b5242e3bed58ef1347d92571b49c7b521a3b0d.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x, y)$ defined on $R$. Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: $M_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion $R_{ij}$*" 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186152401 1071 "![](images/c2/c28d3a6098da6c8be022974e96b5242e3bed58ef1347d92571b49c7b521a3b0d.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186152401 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{12}+{M}_{22} \\\\  & =2{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+2{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186157290 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256658 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186157290 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256683 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186157290 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256708 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186157294 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256751 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162087 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256719 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162087 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256720 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162087 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256721 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162087 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256722 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256731 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256736 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256737 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256739 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256727 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256728 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256729 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256740 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256741 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162333 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159170 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186162333 1068 #edb/ref 17592186255927 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162333 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162333 1071 "![](images/55/558dbbc424725ca0d9bad628968489cc2e32d67136102290666ff055a634bc16.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{C}ds$, where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186162333 1071 "![](images/55/558dbbc424725ca0d9bad628968489cc2e32d67136102290666ff055a634bc16.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162333 1074 "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/82/82fedadbb33b1747832bac25d9cda8e0b6b18b0fab411a870e90bc09ce47226e.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4=2(\\pi +2).\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162337 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159194 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186162337 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256282 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162337 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162337 1071 "![](images/b7/b7e72ce1ab38408f04f3b8d5a228ec0a3632c60086ef0a7abeb7e18af3002e6b.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{C}ds$, where $C$ is the line segment shown above." 13194139533397 17592186045585 false] [17592186162337 1071 "![](images/b7/b7e72ce1ab38408f04f3b8d5a228ec0a3632c60086ef0a7abeb7e18af3002e6b.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the line segment shown above." 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186162337 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256604 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256606 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256607 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256608 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256610 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256612 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186166859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256614 13194139533397 17592186045585 tr