97 17592186045585 false] [17592186167095 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x$ meters, the velocity is given by $v(x)=(1+x)\\,m/s.$ Initially, $P$ is at the origin $O.$ Find $x$ as a function of time $t.$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186167095 1074 "![](images/a8/a8a6f49ead700bee856b1bbdbb10848eac0a57609da14e3967916a36eb56f048.png)\n\nWe're given that the velocity function $v(x)$ is\n\n$$\nv(x)=1+x.\n$$\n\nWe know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1+x.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =1+x \\\\ \\frac{1}{1+x}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1+x}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1+x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x| & =t+K \\\\ 1+x & =C{e}^{t} \\\\ x & =C{e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=1,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{t}-1.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172022 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256386 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172022 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256388 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256379 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256380 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172023 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256382 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256715 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256716 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256718 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172090 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256685 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186172090 1