\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=7+4+4+1=16.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256160 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1069 "q-122965" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-2x-2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3},\\,{P}_{2}={1,2,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1072 #uuid "47dab4f9-83eb-55b5-936b-f3f44a3e6af8" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256764 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/46/46b590842cb6dd1cb994318be3a35ef0f7782542d3a74c4f788180577ab50301.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-2x-2y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-2x-2y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/52/52c19da39a43cdbf1b1d2565669c391e59679b3bf9828f7c46755831b2b0890c.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/2a/2acddf617eda8211e45d281329051f08a8b83788e24b70ebe8d526b58b195bba.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,3)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=5+3+3+1=12.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256040 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1069 "q-122973" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1071 "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,11].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1072 #uuid "366f52d6-db14-505d-8d2d-8b444cdf2898" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256765 1074 "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,11],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =11-4 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256290 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1069 "q-122976" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1071 "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-7,-1].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}.$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1072 #uuid "90442cb7-648a-538a-ae03-0382a8c2214a" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256766 1074 "Note that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[-7,-1],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =(-1)-(-7) \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256152 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1069 "q-122977" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1071 "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}.$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1072 #uuid "108d22ab-96a8-5eeb-96fd-0dcc96561441" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256767 1074 "First, we take the factor $(-4)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}=-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,10],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=(-4)\\cdot 8=-32.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256130 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1069 "q-122979" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1071 "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,9].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}.$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1072 #uuid "99e23ff1-d646-54b7-8668-22a06e7d8b04" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256768 1074 "First, we take the factor $7$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}=7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,9],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}=7\\cdot 5=35.\n$$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186255972 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1069 "q-122982" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1071 "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3,4},\\,{P}_{2}={0,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1072 #uuid "aea78735-0849-5195-bf1a-fcbc0a64996f" 13194139533397 17592186045585 true] [17592186256769 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/c3/c30acb7cb94886e612675d5e64838961134e8d09e5d88c1d803067832f4b173e.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})\n$$\n\